\",\"prefetch\":false,\"className\":\"text-[11px] font-heading uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-text-accent hover:text-text-accent-bright transition-colors\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L4c\",null,{\"k\":\"pages.heroes.rankTierListLink\",\"params\":{\"rank\":\"Legend\"}}],\" →\"]}]]}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-text-muted text-[13px] leading-relaxed\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L4c\",null,{\"k\":\"pages.heroes.rankSentenceLead\",\"params\":{\"rank\":\"Legend\",\"name\":\"Popol and Kupa\"}}],[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"className\":\"text-text-primary\",\"children\":[\"55.33\",\"%\"]}],[\"$\",\"$L4c\",null,{\"k\":\"pages.heroes.rankSentenceMid1\",\"params\":{\"name\":\"Popol and Kupa\",\"delta\":\"+0.67%\"}}],[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"className\":\"text-text-primary\",\"children\":[\"0.51\",\"%\"]}],[\"$\",\"$L4c\",null,{\"k\":\"pages.heroes.rankSentenceMid2\"}],[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"className\":\"text-text-primary\",\"children\":[\"0.42\",\"%\"]}],[\"$\",\"$L4c\",null,{\"k\":\"pages.heroes.rankSentenceAfter\",\"params\":{\"rank\":\"Legend\"}}]]}]]}],[\"$\",\"article\",\"mythic\",{\"className\":\"group relative min-w-0 border border-mlbb-gold/15 bg-surface-1/40 p-3.5 pl-5 md:p-4 md:pl-6 transition-colors hover:border-mlbb-gold/30\",\"children\":[\"$La3\",\"$La4\",\"$La5\"]}],\"$La6\",\"$La7\"]}]\n80:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"h2-1\",{\"className\":\"text-xl md:text-[26px] font-heading font-bold text-[#F0D060] mt-10 mb-4 first:mt-0 text-balance uppercase tracking-[0.04em] leading-tight relative\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"className\":\"block w-10 h-[3px] bg-gradient-to-r from-[#F0D060] to-[#C8AA6E]/0 mb-3\"}],\"The Whole Hero Is A Forced-Path Argument\"]}]\n81:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-4\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"Popol and Kupa only makes sense once you stop reading the kit as \\\"marksman plus pet\\\" and start reading it as a forced-path argument. He does not win because his autos are prettier than everyone else's. He wins because he makes one enemy solve the fight in the wrong order.\"}]\n82:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-5\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"code\",\"code-0\",{\"className\":\"px-1.5 py-0.5 bg-[#000000] border border-[#C8AA6E]/15 text-[#F0D060] font-mono text-[0.85em]\",\"children\":\"Bite 'em, Kupa!\"}],\" decides who the game is about. Once the tag lands, Kupa locks on and the trade stops being clean. The target now has to answer Kupa, Popol's empowered next basic, and whatever trap line was already planted behind the exchange. During ultimate, that same catch becomes a real stun and the window gets short fast. This is why Popol feels oppressive when ahead and fake when behind: if the tag matters, the whole kit matters. If it does not, you are just a short-range marksman babysitting a dog.\"]}]\n83:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-6\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"code\",\"code-0\",{\"className\":\"px-1.5 py-0.5 bg-[#000000] border border-[#C8AA6E]/15 text-[#F0D060] font-mono text-[0.85em]\",\"children\":\"Kupa, Help!\"}],\" is the spell that keeps the hero playable into melee pressure. It is your peel, your shield, your way to drag Kupa back through a diver, and in Alpha Wolf form it briefly breaks the enemy's rhythm with an airborne. Most weak Popol games come from spending this skill for decorative damage before the real engage starts. Once it is gone, every assassin on the map knows exactly how honest your body is.\"]}]\n84:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-7\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"code\",\"code-0\",{\"className\":\"px-1.5 py-0.5 bg-[#000000] border border-[#C8AA6E]/15 text-[#F0D060] font-mono text-[0.85em]\",\"children\":\"Popol's Surprise\"}],\" is the real draft reason to pick him. The trap is not there to pad damage. It tells both teams where the fight is allowed to happen. A trap on the river mouth changes the lane. A trap on the jungle hinge changes the invade. A trap behind your own lane changes the dive angle. If you place traps after contact, you are already late.\"]}]\n85:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-8\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"The ultimate is not a button you press because it is glowing. It fully restores Kupa, upgrades both command skills, and gives Popol the movement speed to keep the exchange connected. Use it when Kupa has already taken contact and the target cannot simply walk away. The reset is free value only if the fight is already real.\"}]\n86:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"h2-2\",{\"className\":\"text-xl md:text-[26px] font-heading font-bold text-[#F0D060] mt-10 mb-4 first:mt-0 text-balance uppercase tracking-[0.04em] leading-tight relative\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"className\":\"block w-10 h-[3px] bg-gradient-to-r from-[#F0D060] to-[#C8AA6E]/0 mb-3\"}],\"Laning: the first four minutes\"]}]\n87:[\"$\",\"ol\",\"ol-0\",{\"className\":\"list-decimal list-inside text-[#9BA0B4] my-3 space-y-2 ml-2\",\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":[\"Take \",[\"$\",\"code\",\"code-0\",{\"className\":\"px-1.5 py-0.5 bg-[#000000] border border-[#C8AA6E]/15 text-[#F0D060] font-mono text-[0.85em]\",\"children\":\"Bite 'em, Kupa!\"}],\" first and claim one brush.\"]}],\" Tag the enemy gold laner once, let Kupa walk them backward, and then return the wave to a spot where your brush still matters. The point is not a level 1 all-in. The point is teaching the opponent that last-hitting on your side of the lane costs health.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-1\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Freeze toward your trap, not toward your tower.\"}],\" Popol's strongest early lane is the one where the enemy has to choose between stepping into a river trap or giving up space. Hard shoving every wave wastes the hero's best tool and invites the exact gank path your trap should have denied.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-2\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Save battle-spell tempo for the first real collapse.\"}],\" Flicker is not an opening flourish. Hold it for the 2:00 to 3:00 window when the jungler can actually convert on you, or for the first level-4 punish where a trapped target has already spent movement. If you are jungling, the same rule applies to Retribution tempo around first objective setups.\"]}],\"\\n\"]}]\n88:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-9\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"The lane plan is simple on paper and demanding in practice. Keep Kupa healthy enough to threaten, keep one trap covering the path that matters most, and trade only when the enemy has to walk through your prep to reach Popol. If you start taking open-field trades because you feel ahead, the lane stops belonging to you.\"}]\n89:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"h2-3\",{\"className\":\"text-xl md:text-[26px] font-heading font-bold text-[#F0D060] mt-10 mb-4 first:mt-0 text-balance uppercase tracking-[0.04em] leading-tight relative\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"className\":\"block w-10 h-[3px] bg-gradient-to-r from-[#F0D060] to-[#C8AA6E]/0 mb-3\"}],\"The Two-Item Window That Turns Picks Into Towers\"]}]\n8a:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-10\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":[\"The two-item spike that matters most is \",[\"$\",\"code\",\"code-0\",{\"className\":\"px-1.5 py-0.5 bg-[#000000] border border-[#C8AA6E]/15 text-[#F0D060] font-mono text-[0.85em]\",\"children\":\"Blade of Despair\"}],\" plus \",[\"$\",\"code\",\"code-1\",{\"className\":\"px-1.5 py-0.5 bg-[#000000] border border-[#C8AA6E]/15 text-[#F0D060] font-mono text-[0.85em]\",\"children\":\"Demon Hunter Sword\"}],\", usually around the 7 to 9 minute mark in an even game.\"]}]\n8b:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-11\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"code\",\"code-0\",{\"className\":\"px-1.5 py-0.5 bg-[#000000] border border-[#C8AA6E]/15 text-[#F0D060] font-mono text-[0.85em]\",\"children\":\"Blade of Despair\"}],\" gives Popol the raw threat his catches need. Once a target is already chunked or trapped, the extra physical attack against enemies below half HP turns a clean catch into a real kill window. \",[\"$\",\"code\",\"code-1\",{\"className\":\"px-1.5 py-0.5 bg-[#000000] border border-[#C8AA6E]/15 text-[#F0D060] font-mono text-[0.85em]\",\"children\":\"Demon Hunter Sword\"}],\" solves the second half of the problem by adding current-HP damage on basic attacks and on-hit sustain, which means Popol can keep firing while Kupa keeps the target busy. One item makes the punish scary. The other makes the punish survive contact.\"]}]\n8c:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-12\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"This is the timing where your catches should start producing structures, not just health bars. Before these two items, a trapped target often means space and lane control. After these two items, the same catch should become a tower plate, Turtle entry, jungle camp, or outer turret. If you are still spending the whole mid game farming side waves after this spike, you are late to the hero's best phase.\"}]\n8d:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-13\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"Mechanically, nothing magical changed except the cost of stepping wrong. Popol already had vision and target lock. Now the target actually dies for disrespecting either one. That is why this spike is strongest in tight spaces. Jungle entrances, Turtle corridors, and tower approaches magnify both items. Long open chases do not.\"}]\n8e:[\"$\",\"$La8\",null,{\"slot\":\"7246933188\",\"variant\":\"in-article\",\"className\":\"my-8\"}]\n8f:[[\"$\",\"h2\",\"h2-0\",{\"className\":\"text-xl md:text-[26px] font-heading font-bold text-[#F0D060] mt-10 mb-4 first:mt-0 text-balance uppercase tracking-[0.04em] leading-tight relative\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"className\":\"block w-10 h-[3px] bg-gradient-to-r from-[#F0D060] to-[#C8AA6E]/0 mb-3\"}],\"Teamfight Positioning Means Playing Behind The Dog\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"The common bad reflex is to let Kupa hit the nearest tank and call that target priority. That is lazy Popol play. Your first target is the hero whose movement you can actually deny right now. Sometimes that is the frontliner. Often it is the diver who already spent a dash, the mage who entered your trap line, or the marksman who arrived late through a narrow angle.\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"ol\",\"ol-0\",{\"className\":\"list-decimal list-inside text-[#9BA0B4] my-3 space-y-2 ml-2\",\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Stand one layer behind your first engager, not beside Kupa.\"}],\" Kupa is the front edge of the exchange. Popol should be one step behind the hero buying space, close enough to keep the tag connected and far enough that \",[\"$\",\"code\",\"code-0\",{\"className\":\"px-1.5 py-0.5 bg-[#000000] border border-[#C8AA6E]/15 text-[#F0D060] font-mono text-[0.85em]\",\"children\":\"Kupa, Help!\"}],\" still peels through the first diver.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-1\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Trap exits before the engage, not under the brawl.\"}],\" A trap on the retreat path keeps the catch going. A trap dropped directly under five bodies usually lands too late to matter. Pre-plant the way out, then make the enemy choose it.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-2\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Ultimate after contact, not on sight.\"}],\" \",[\"$\",\"code\",\"code-0\",{\"className\":\"px-1.5 py-0.5 bg-[#000000] border border-[#C8AA6E]/15 text-[#F0D060] font-mono text-[0.85em]\",\"children\":\"We Are Angry!\"}],\" is strongest once Kupa has already taken some damage and the target has committed. You get the full reset, the upgraded stun, and the movement speed window at the exact moment the enemy thought the trade was stabilizing.\"]}],\"\\n\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-1\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"The support-dependent edge case is straightforward. If your roam or pocket support can safely extend your chase, you can step farther after the first trap triggers and trust the follow-up. If your backline help is slower or purely reactive, keep the fight local and cash the catch quickly. Popol looks brave only while Kupa and peel are both available.\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"h2\",\"h2-1\",{\"className\":\"text-xl md:text-[26px] font-heading font-bold text-[#F0D060] mt-10 mb-4 first:mt-0 text-balance uppercase tracking-[0.04em] leading-tight relative\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"className\":\"block w-10 h-[3px] bg-gradient-to-r from-[#F0D060] to-[#C8AA6E]/0 mb-3\"}],\"Itemization: Build A Spine, Then Solve The Threat\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-2\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"Think of Popol's build as a spine plus answers.\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-3\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":[\"Start with \",[\"$\",\"code\",\"code-0\",{\"className\":\"px-1.5 py-0.5 bg-[#000000] border border-[#C8AA6E]/15 text-[#F0D060] font-mono text-[0.85em]\",\"children\":\"Swift Boots\"}],\" in gold lane unless the matchup forces defensive boots immediately. The attack speed matters because Popol needs his empowered basic attacks to arrive on time once Kupa has claimed the target. In jungle, the boot conversation becomes your Retribution upgrade, but the rest of the logic stays similar.\"]}],\"\\n\",\"$La9\",\"\\n\",\"$Laa\",\"\\n\",\"$Lab\",\"\\n\",\"$Lac\",\"\\n\",\"$Lad\",\"\\n\",\"$Lae\",\"\\n\",\"$Laf\",\"\\n\",\"$Lb0\",\"\\n\",\"$Lb1\",\"\\n\",\"$Lb2\",\"\\n\",\"$Lb3\",\"\\n\",\"$Lb4\",\"\\n\",\"$Lb5\",\"\\n\",\"$Lb6\",\"\\n\",\"$Lb7\",\"\\n\",\"$Lb8\"]\n90:[\"$\",\"$Lb9\",null,{\"heroName\":\"Popol and Kupa\"}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"91:[\"$\",\"$L6c\",\"carmilla\",{\"href\":\"/heroes/carmilla\",\"className\":\"group block\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"relative bg-surface-4 border border-mlbb-gold/20 overflow-hidden card-hover hover:border-mlbb-gold/50\",\"style\":{\"boxShadow\":\"0 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.3)\"},\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex items-center gap-3 p-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"relative w-14 h-14 rounded-full overflow-hidden flex-shrink-0 bg-surface-3\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L6d\",null,{\"src\":\"https://akmweb.youngjoygame.com/web/svnres/img/test/homepage_2_2_16_1232_1/100_6fb8f120dafdcbc1b5da2a2667016ad5.png\",\"alt\":\"Carmilla - Shadow of Twilight\",\"unoptimized\":false,\"priority\":\"$undefined\",\"fetchPriority\":\"$undefined\",\"fill\":true,\"className\":\"object-cover group-hover:scale-110 transition-transform duration-300\",\"sizes\":\"56px\",\"placeholder\":\"blur\",\"blurDataURL\":\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB3aWR0aD0iMTAwIiBoZWlnaHQ9IjEwMCIgeG1sbnM9Imh0dHA6Ly93d3cudzMub3JnLzIwMDAvc3ZnIj48cmVjdCB3aWR0aD0iMTAwIiBoZWlnaHQ9IjEwMCIgZmlsbD